   <!--
   =====================================================================
   ALASKA (AK) - NO STATE INCOME TAX TEST CASE
   =====================================================================

   Alaska has NO state income tax on any type of income:
   - W-2 wages: NOT TAXED
   - Investment income: NOT TAXED
   - Self-employment income: NOT TAXED
   - Capital gains: NOT TAXED

   Alaska is one of 9 states with no personal income tax.
   Instead, the state relies on oil revenues and other taxes.

   This test case validates:
   - High W-2 income ($120,000) is NOT taxed
   - Investment income (dividends + interest) is NOT taxed
   - State tax = $0 regardless of income amount or type

   Income breakdown:
   - W-2 wages: $120,000
   - Qualified dividends: $8,000
   - Interest income: $2,000
   - Total income: $130,000

   Expected Results:
   - Federal AGI: $130,000
   - Federal Taxable: ~$115,000 (after standard deduction)
   - Federal Tax: ~$21,000 (approximate, with preferential dividend rate)
   - AK State Tax: $0 (no income tax)
   =====================================================================
   -->

